Rent the Runway enables subscribers to rent designer apparel and accessories, building a 5-20 item 'closet' with 1-4 swaps monthly. The model shifts ownership to access, expanding wardrobe variety while reducing consumption pressure on fashion production. Since 2022, RTR has offset 100% of shipment carbon through renewable energy and uses 100% reusable, compostable, or recyclable packaging. The company has mastered garment care through 15 years of cleaning and repair expertise, returning items in pristine condition. However, Finnish LCA research reveals shipping logistics generate substantial emissions—97% of the model's footprint from postal deliveries and returns. Rent the Runway demonstrates both the potential and limitations of access-based models, highlighting how logistics infrastructure remains critical to circular viability.